 "post": {
  "title": "Why Your Wobbly Shelf Feels Priceless #shorts",
  "description": "Nia spent six hours on a wobbly shelf and won't sell it for less than a new one costs. Psychologists call it the IKEA effect. Michael Norton, Daniel Mochon and Dan Ariely (\"The IKEA effect: When labor leads to love\", Journal of Consumer Psychology, 2012) had people assemble plain IKEA storage boxes: builders were willing to pay 63% more for their box than people handed the same box already built. The effect also showed up for origami and Lego, and it depended on actually finishing the build. #psychology #shorts #ikeaeffect #behavioraleconomics",
